#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# series_coefficient

#% text
# `series_coefficient(s, k)` gives the coefficient of order k of the series s; `series_coefficient(s, [k1, k2, ...])` of a series in several variables.

#% text
# `series_coefficient(f, [x, x0, k])` gives the coefficient of (x - x0)^k in the expansion of f; further specifications take coefficients in further variables.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# With a symbolic k the general coefficient is given for sums of terms c x^m h(x) with h one of exp, sin, cos, sinh, cosh of a linear function and a power of a linear function; it holds for the integers k >= m.

#% item
# Orders below the first term give 0, orders beyond the truncation of the series `indeterminate`.

#% item
# The order k must be an exact integer.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
series_coefficient(series(exp(sin(x)), x, 0, 10), 8)
#% output
#= 31/5760

#% cell
series_coefficient(1/(1 - t - t^2), [t, 0, 10])
#% output
#= 89

#% cell
series_coefficient(exp(x + y), [x, 0, 3], [y, 0, 3])
#% output
#= 1/36

#% cell
series_coefficient(sin(x), [x, pi, 3])
#% output
#= 1/6

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `series`, `coefficient`, `normal`
